# Phase 3 inline-fingerprint dedup microbench — issue #41 Chunk 1
#
# Compares the new `InlineDedupTable` primitive against the Phase 1
# `dedup_samples_streaming` (two_hash_cuckoo with indices-only slots)
# and the production packed-key sort default.
#
# Bench: jxl-encoder/benches/dedup_samples_strategies.rs
# Primitive: jxl-encoder/src/modular/inline_dedup_table.rs
# Run: cargo bench -p jxl-encoder --features __bench_internals \
#                  --bench dedup_samples_strategies -- --group=<group>
#
# Bench harness was extended with three new bench paths:
#   * inline_dedup_prebuilt   — algorithm-only (keys built up front)
#   * gather_sim_phase1       — Phase 1 cache pattern (lazy key build,
#                                indices-only slots, SoA chase verify)
#   * gather_sim_phase3       — Phase 3 cache pattern (lazy key build,
#                                fingerprint-cache slots, compact
#                                unique_keys verify)
#
# Hardware: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (water-cooled, no thermal throttling)
# Toolchain: rustc 1.95.0 stable, default codegen, no target-cpu=native
# Build: cargo build --release (jxl-encoder/.cargo/config defaults)
# Features used: __bench_internals
#
# Raw bench output: inline_dedup_microbench_2026-05-17.txt
# Clean re-run (after killing orphan bench process that locked the
# first run's small-N groups): inline_dedup_microbench_clean_2026-05-17.txt
#
# Clean-run results (gather_sim Phase 3 vs Phase 1, Mops/s):
#
#   group              | phase1 | phase3 | delta
#   -------------------|--------|--------|------
#   200K_dup600        |  4.79  |  5.03  |  +5 %
#   200K_dup800        |  2.88  |  3.89  | +35 %
#   1.35M_dup300       |  2.42  |  3.70  | +53 %
#   1.35M_dup600       |  2.53  |  3.53  | +40 %
#   1.35M_dup800       |  2.75  |  3.73  | +36 %
#
# Acceptance gate ("phase3 > phase1") met by +5 % to +53 % across all
# tested (n, dup-ratio) cells, with the larger wins concentrated at
# realistic sample counts and dup ratios (where the SoA chase cost
# Phase 1 paid dominates probe wall-clock).
#
# Phase 3 still trails the packed-key sort post-pass on the synthetic
# uncorrelated-byte input — the bench's make_samples produces no
# spatial-locality clustering, which the sort path exploits via
# packed-key cmp short-circuit. Chunk 2's production wiring is what
# captures the gather-time win on real photo data.
